# .gitignore for a D&D data dir (written by the dnd-dm plugin when it creates the
# dir; see "Saving Campaigns" in the dnd-dm:new-campaign skill).

# Imported PDF/homebrew rulebooks (can be large) and the regenerable SRD cache
# (bin/dm20 seeds it from the plugin).
library/
rulebook_cache/

# --- Campaign data: kept out of git by default -------------------------------
# Campaign data (characters, the DM's secret arc and other spoilers, session
# notes) stays out of git unless you choose otherwise, so a push of this project
# can't publish your game. Remove these two lines to back campaigns up in this
# repo, ideally after making the repo private. Either way, campaigns ignored
# here are NOT backed up.
campaigns
events

# --- Always ignored, even if you remove the block above ----------------------
# party/ holds the secret player-link tokens, QR codes and live feed
# (committing them would publish working join credentials); voice_registry.yaml
# is regenerated per session; the per-campaign rulebook cache is regenerable.
campaigns/*/party/
campaigns/*/voice_registry.yaml
campaigns/*/rulebooks/cache/
